# Container

`src/container.ts` is the composition root. It instantiates repositories, adapters, and use-cases once, then exports `container`. Routers call `container.{context}.{verb}.execute(...)`.

One repository instance per aggregate is shared by the use-cases and the adapter of that aggregate.

## Do

- `new Repository()`, `new Adapter(repository)`, `new UseCase(...)`
- Pass an adapter where a use-case expects a port
- Group use-cases on `container.{context}`

## Don't

- Build port objects in this file
- `new` in routers or use-cases
- Rebuild the container inside a transaction — call `port.withTx(tx)` / `repository.withTx(tx)`

```ts
const membershipRepository = new MembershipRepository();
const membershipAdapter = new MembershipAdapter(membershipRepository);
const findMembership = new FindMembershipUseCase(membershipRepository);

export const container = {
  membership: { findMembership },
};
```
